Title: Session memory lands uncommitted and silently stalls host harness pulls
Created: 2026-09-29
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-09-29T12:59Z claude created from /roar sweep; related to 0978 (relocation) and 0987 (idh sync)

2026-10-01T19:03Z MinhHaDuong codex note Removed the obsolete 0978 coupling: 0999 portability does not decide whether session memory remains in the pulled tree.
--- body ---

## Context

Claude Code writes native project memory into `projects/*/memory/` inside the
harness checkout, the same tree the nightly pull fast-forwards. Nothing commits
those writes. When an incoming commit touches the same path, the pull refuses
and keeps refusing, with no signal a person sees.

Observed 2026-09-29: padme's `claude-harness-pull` had failed every night since
2026-09-24 on 3 new and 1 edited memory notes plus two index lines, leaving the
host 134 commits behind — including the destructive-bash guard wiring. Rescued
by PR #1057 (3-way merge, union of index conflicts), byte-verified before the
local copies were discarded. The same afternoon doudou's primary checkout held
3 modified and 4 new memory files from other live sessions.

`idh sync` (0987) will name the blocking files, which makes the stall visible
but does not prevent it. The portable `~/.agents` clone contract in 0999
changes how the checkout is found, not whether memory writes are committed.

## Options

1. Pull tolerates memory: rebase/autostash only `projects/*/memory/`, or merge
   with a union driver for `MEMORY.md` (index files are append-mostly).
2. Memory writes land as commits: a SessionEnd step (or `/lair`) commits and
   opens a memory-only PR, as the 2026-09-29 rescue did by hand.
3. Memory leaves the pulled tree, with its own sync. This is a memory ownership
   decision, not part of the repository portability work in 0999.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A host whose sessions wrote memory since the last pull still fast-forwards the harness the next night, in a disposable-HOME reproduction of the padme case (positive control: today's script refuses)
- [ ] No memory note is lost or duplicated across the reproduction (byte comparison of the note set before and after)
- [ ] A pull that still cannot proceed is reported where the author sees it (session start or `idh status`), not only in a journal
- [ ] `make check` passes
